2b:Tc05,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://www.raulji.com/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Gujarat","item":"https://www.raulji.com/gujarat/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":3,"name":"Surat","item":"https://www.raulji.com/surat/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":4,"name":"LLP","item":"https://www.raulji.com/surat/llp-registration/"}]},{"@type":"Service","@id":"https://www.raulji.com/surat/llp-registration/#service","name":"LLP Registration in Surat","description":"For most Surat firms thinking about changing structure, the LLP is the answer they should be looking at first, and often are not. The city's diamond and textile trades run on thousands of partnership firms with two, three or four working partners. What is increasingly uncomfortable about that is not the partner arrangement, which works, but the unlimited personal liability that comes with it.","url":"https://www.raulji.com/surat/llp-registration/","serviceType":"LLP Registration","provider":{"@id":"https://www.raulji.com/#organization"},"areaServed":{"@type":"City","name":"Surat","containedInPlace":{"@type":"AdministrativeArea","name":"Surat district, Gujarat"}},"offers":{"@type":"Offer","priceCurrency":"INR","price":"7999","description":"One-time professional fee. Government filing fees and the stamp duty on the LLP Agreement are charged separately and vary by state and contribution.","url":"https://www.raulji.com/surat/llp-registration/"}},{"@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Is an LLP better than a company for a Surat textile firm?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"For most of them, yes, provided there is no plan to raise equity. An LLP caps personal liability, keeps the partner structure and profit shares intact, appears on the MCA register where banks and buyers can verify it, and avoids statutory audit from year one. A company only becomes the better answer when you need to issue shares or a specific counterparty insists on one."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What happens to our existing partnership deed when we convert?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Its commercial substance moves into the LLP Agreement, which becomes the governing document and must be filed in Form 3 within thirty days of incorporation. This is a good opportunity to settle the things the old deed left vague, typically exit terms, what happens on a partner's death, and who may commit the business to credit."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Will our bank accept an LLP for our working capital facility?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Banks lend to LLPs routinely, and the LLP's presence on the MCA register with filed annual accounts generally helps rather than hinders a credit assessment. What you should not assume is that an existing facility transfers automatically. The LLP is a new entity with a new PAN, so the facility has to be re-documented, and that is worth starting before the conversion rather than after."}}]}]}21:[["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$2b"}}],["$","nav",null,{"aria-label":"Breadcrumb","className":"container-wide pt-28 md:pt-32","children":"$L2c"}],"$L2d","$L2e","$L2f","$L30","$L31","$L32","$L33","$L34"]
